  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced vocational training for increased employability of the target groups.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite some progress on indicators related to child and maternal health, Mozambique is lagging on most of the SDG targets related to human development. In fact, Mozambique has regressed in the global human development ranking, with strong disparities among regions. While significant progress was made on national social protection programmes and safety nets, social protection is not yet comprehensive enough to provide adequate coverage for all and protect an already impoverished population from extreme poverty and recurrent shocks. 
Lifelong learning is a key to building human capital, innovation and competitiveness in a globalized, fast-changing world. Most learning takes place through non-formal and informal means, whether at work, home, or elsewhere. In Mozambique, most people acquire workplace skills by informal means. In the absence of recognized qualifications, they face severe disadvantages as far as finding decent jobs, migrating to other countries within the region and accessing further education and training. Unfortunately, most formal education and training systems are not geared to recognize non-formal and informal learning. This not only hinders the development of work force but is also a cause of its under-utilization. As a result, the recognition of knowledge, skills and competencies acquired through non-formal and informal means is becoming a highly aspirational, political and social issue, attracting the attention of government.
To implement R208 on quality apprenticeship programme Structured apprenticeship programmes are increasingly recognized as key policy tools to facilitate the transitions of young people from school to employment. Quality apprenticeships offer young people direct work experience, as well as applied knowledge and skills. This combination enables apprentices to understand the logic behind the job they are tasked with, cope with unpredictable situations, and acquire higher level/transferable skills. In addition, apprenticeship</narrative>
  </description>
